 ## Project Roles
 
+### Contributor
+Contributors submit pull requests, documentation updates, and bug fixes.
+
 ### Steering Member
 Steering members guide project direction and review architectural changes.
+Members participate in bi-weekly governance meetings.
 
 ### Release Operator
 Release operators manage deployment pipelines and production rollouts.
+The release operator role is normatively defined in teams.yaml, which deployment automation validates before promoting builds.
+Operators must coordinate major version cuts across `#queue-releases`.
 
 ### Triage Contributor
 Triage contributors organize issues, reproduce bugs, and manage labels.
+New contributors are encouraged to start with triage tasks.
+
+## Role Onboarding
+1. Request membership through an issue template.
+2. Complete security review and two-factor authentication setup.
+3. Receive approval from at least one steering member.
 
